{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792424439,"nonce":"W6ol+YStIaEFW5vJVv8sq2rX2So=","message":"Backdrop records are in 10c800a10969a68be2748cc32b8a9e0f0dd9e53b (local, not pushed), tracked separately by 15d62ffc9c5aa3e7e0959a3992c0267c31ee5065f0a1510b34f4832b8e3f5aea. Kind::Backdrop and Item::Backdrop retain the record's logical rows, display scale and element-frame shape payload. Record::backdrop reads and validates it, rejecting non-finite data and negative blur/read margins as BackdropEffect before constructing Gaussian weights; primitive-only decoding still names kind 42 as requiring an ordered pass.\n\nPainter snapshots the pixels painted so far at each backdrop, so overlapping backdrops and intervening primitives retain paint order. Plans containing backdrops draw into a pooled copyable frame and finish with a raw premultiplied copy to the caller's target, which needs only RENDER_ATTACHMENT usage. Layers containing a backdrop retain the full sampling frame and a transparent sampling root. Ordinary plans retain their previous direct path. The read region includes the producer's transformed expanded quad, read margin and a small physical sampling fringe. The final backdrop is rasterized as that expanded quad, which bounds coverage under strongly anisotropic transforms.\n\nThe new pass applies a separable full-resolution Gaussian in premultiplied pixels, the record's matrix in straight colour, opacity and grain. Liquid glass carries its signed bevel, rim line, lighting, tint, explicit border, refraction, dispersion and transparent-source environment. Zero rim widths stay finite while preserving lens effects. Screen, local, fade and element-frame clips, shaped corners and notches use the shared distance and clip helpers. Gaussian tap pairs moved into display_list::gaussian and remain shared with the unchanged layer effects; variable-length backdrop taps and shape points use a uniform plus a nonfilterable auxiliary texture, with no shader storage requirement. Native glass pipelines, GpuPrimitive (544 bytes), GpuImageInstance (208 bytes), the ABI schema, shared ClipPath enum and CSS keywords are unchanged.\n\nNineteen scenes, each encoded at scales 1 and 2 by blinc_abi a92f5c0, cover zero and wider blur, frosted grain, liquid refraction and dispersion, explicit borders and inset bevels, transparent sources, general and strongly anisotropic affines, notches, screen/local/fade/polygon/ellipse clips, nested filtered layers, overlapping backdrops with an intervening foreground box, a non-diagonal CSS matrix, zero bevel, zero rim width and viewport-edge clamping. Six GPU-free tests cover record units, matrices and glass parameters, clips and truncated polygon tails, ordering/layer nesting, invalid kinds/degenerate transforms, and invalid numeric data. Both shaders pass Naga validation and uniform layout checks.\n\nOffscreen Apple M1 Pro, Metal: all 25 display-list GPU tests and the polygon fill-rule test pass. A single Painter is reused across the backdrop scenes to exercise cached resources and changing sizes/parameters. A separate target with only RENDER_ATTACHMENT usage passes. Against an independent CPU oracle, worst whole-frame error across all four channels is 1/255 except frosted grain at 2/255. The oracle samples the full source frame, uses a dense Gaussian for rows and derives fractional vertical fetches independently from those weights. Only the rotated polygon clip excludes discontinuous boundary probes: 1 of 24,000 pixels at scale 1, 2 of 96,000 at scale 2, using the existing 0.001 logical-pixel guard. All other backdrop scenes skip none.\n\nThe forced vertex-buffer path passes all 25 tests. With both storage capability flags temporarily disabled and BLINC_GPU_MAX_PRIMITIVES=1024 BLINC_GPU_MAX_GLYPHS=1024, the backdrop/image subset also passes on Metal: 17 scenes at both scales plus the render-only target. Only the two scenes using ordinary SDF primitives, nested layers and overlapping order, are excluded from that forced data-texture run because ce34b20 still tracks stale SDF packing. Every capability and test override was restored. Actual WebGL2, PowerVR/Adreno compilation and mobile pixels remain unverified. Backdrop blur stays full resolution; no performance claims or half-resolution approximation are made here.\n\nMutation checks fail by 119/255 for reversed paint order, 4/255 for removing the read margin, 47/255 for seeding a layer with its parent's pixels, 88/255 for disabling dispersion, and 18/255 for oversizing the expanded quad. Restored tests pass. Oracle corrections: a dense integer vertical convolution initially differed by 10/255 under refraction even though the offsets agreed. The reference samples paired Gaussian fetches after fractional refraction, which differs from interpolating a dense result; the shader formula was retained and the oracle now models those fetches from independently computed weights. The stretch fixture uses a fractional affine translation because layout rounds positions, avoiding a quad edge exactly through sample centres without excluding pixels or relaxing tolerance.\n\nGate: fmt, workspace clippy without new warnings, 1,894 workspace nextest tests (51 skipped), docs with warnings denied, wasm, iOS and threaded layout/CN tests pass. The separate DSL run has 516 passed, 28 failed, 10 skipped; every failing name matches the untouched ff83adca baseline already recorded under a33d2b9. No dependency or DSL sources changed. This completes the scoped backdrop issue; the parent fa2406c remains open for canvases, image mappings, colour glyph work and remaining fallbacks. Next: agree on the canvas consumer API before implementation.","files":null}]}